&lt;p&gt;Frequently cited statistics show that people who identify with historically marginalized groups are likely to apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. We encourage you to help us break that statistic and apply even if you don’t meet every single qualification—your potential is what matters most to us.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoLab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoLab, we help mechanical engineering teams bring life-changing products to market years sooner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoLab is the AI platform for driving stronger engineering decisions. Every design review in CoLab builds a knowledge repository of design feedback, decisions, and lessons learned - which AI agents draw from to flag issues on future designs before they compound. The more your team works in CoLab, the smarter it gets and the faster you arrive at the ideal design. Companies like Ford, Komatsu, and Johnson Controls use CoLab to catch issues earlier, eliminate rework cycles, and bring products to market faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in St. John’s, Newfoundland, CoLab has grown quickly from our first customer in 2019 to a rapidly scaling company. We’ve recently been recognized on Deloitte’s Fast 50™ and Fast 500™, and named a Canadian company to watch by The Globe and Mail and Financial Post.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll take ownership of our US-based cloud infrastructure across both Commercial and Public Sector environments, including our FedRAMP High authorized environment in AWS GovCloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role focused on operating, securing, and scaling a production system supporting regulated workloads. You’ll work inside highly controlled environments, contribute directly to infrastructure and application reliability, and help maintain our FedRAMP authorization through ongoing continuous monitoring (ConMon), security operations, and audit readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also partner closely with third-party vendors and internal teams to support customer onboarding, system improvements, and ongoing compliance requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What success looks like in your first 90 Days:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;30 Days: You’ve passed onboarding, completed security training, contributed code and are comfortable working across both Commercial and Public Sector environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;60 Days: You’re contributing a substantial amount of code (Terraform, Python), reviewing others&#39; work, and managing tasks in the Public Sector environment independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;90 Days: You’re operating independently across Commercial and Public Sector environments, proactively identifying and resolving issues, contributing to system reliability, and supporting ongoing compliance and monitoring activities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Ideal Candidate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a senior engineer with deep hands-on cloud experience who is comfortable writing infrastructure as code, navigating complex environments, and adapting to a security-first approach. You bring technical depth and the curiosity to learn our unique systems and constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll thrive here if you:Have a security-first approach to solving problems or designing solutionsHave a strong point of view on how cloud infrastructure should be managed and a bias for clean, auditable codeCan dive into unknowns, break down stack traces, and own infrastructure problems end-to-endAre comfortable in ambiguity and thrive in a “figure-it-out” environmentHave a self-starter attitude but know that you have a team to support you if you need help&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and operate CoLab’s US-based cloud infrastructure, including our FedRAMP High authorized GovCloud environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ongoing continuous monitoring (ConMon) activities, including vulnerability remediation, logging, and audit readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal and external stakeholders to maintain compliance posture and support audits and assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to scaling infrastructure to support customer onboarding in regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain Terraform to support infrastructure deployments via SpaceLiftBuild and troubleshoot Lambda functions (primarily in Python) to support application and infrastructure automationInvestigate stack traces, diagnose application issues, and contribute to monitoring improvements (especially in APM tracing via DataDog)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the broader Platform Team with secure, scalable infrastructure design and implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Third Party Vendors during the Public Sector implementation and assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contribute to internal codebases (Python + IaC) and participate in PR reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on and eventually lead technical initiatives in Public Sector infrastructure and deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must-Haves:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a hands-on DevOps, Platform, or CloudOps engineering roleDeep experience with AWS (GovCloud preferred) and strong Terraform fluencyProficiency with Python (especially writing Lambda functions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CI/CD tooling and secure deployment practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging skills and comfortability in analyzing logs, traces, and error stacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizenship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-expired US Passport or State issued RealID Drivers License&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SpaceLift or similar Terraform orchestration tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Okta for Government, Azure GCC High, or Google CloudDataDog and/or Cloudflare configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in regulated environments (e.g. FedRAMP, GovCloud, IL4/IL5)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security controls, audit processes, and continuous monitoring practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to managed dependencies and security patching workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Cypress for automated testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extra Details:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Remote-first (US only), with flexibility around timezone alignment. Some occasional coordination with Canadian teammates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Type: Full-time, permanent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits:Extended health coverage, unlimited paid vacation, equity in a high-growth company,&amp;nbsp;401K matching&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Frequently cited statistics show that people who identify with historically marginalized groups are likely to apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. We encourage you to help us break that statistic and apply even if you don’t meet every single qualification, your potential is what matters most to us.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoLab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;At CoLab, we help mechanical engineering teams bring life-changing products to market years sooner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;We build AI for engineers designing cars, medical devices, and jet engines. Products this complex aren&#39;t sketched and sent to production. Teams spend months on iterations, reviews, and tests, predicting how every part performs before anything is built. CoLab is where those reviews happen, and we capture the rationale behind every change. Other tools show what changed between versions. Only CoLab knows why. That&#39;s how our AI helps manufacturers like Bobcat, Triumph Motorcycles, and GE Appliances make better decisions, eliminate rework cycles, and get to market faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Proudly based in St. John’s, Newfoundland, CoLab started with one customer in 2018. Since then we’ve raised a $72M Series C, been named the 57th fastest growing company in North America by Deloitte (Fast 500™), signed multi-year AI partnerships with companies like Bombardier, and grown to a team of 250+.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re building out CoLab&#39;s commercial product in AWS GovCloud to serve customers with stringent security and compliance requirements. We&#39;re looking for an exceptional full stack engineer to help make it happen.&lt;br&gt;As one of the first Software Developers on our FedRAMP team, you&#39;ll own significant portions of this effort end-to-end. From architecture decisions to backend services, databases, and frontend experiences, you&#39;ll be responsible for turning a complex technical vision into a working product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;This isn&#39;t a role where you&#39;ll inherit a neatly defined backlog. You&#39;ll need to navigate ambiguity, make sound technical decisions, and write production-quality code across the stack. The scope is substantial, the constraints are real, and your work will directly shape how CoLab serves an entirely new segment of customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Ideal Candidate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;re a deeply technical builder who thrives when given ownership of a difficult problem. You&#39;re equally comfortable designing backend systems, building frontend features, and working through unfamiliar infrastructure challenges.You don&#39;t need someone to break a large initiative into tickets for you. You can define the path forward, communicate tradeoffs, and bring others along.&amp;nbsp;You balance speed with engineering discipline, and you&#39;re comfortable being accountable for the outcome—not just your portion of the code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead analysis and development efforts required to bring CoLab’s commercial product features into our FedRAMP Class D (High) certified application, hosted in AWS GovCloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build across our stack: React, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct technical designs that balance security, scalability, maintainability, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate FedRAMP requirements into practical engineering solutions alongside security and compliance partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take complex compliance challenges from technical discovery through implementation, testing, and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish engineering patterns and foundations that future FedRAMP team members can build upon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience building and shipping complex, production-grade SaaS applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and implementing solutions requiring FIPS 140-3 validated cryptography and hardening apps for regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise across frontend and backend development, including React, TypeScript, Python, and PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong AWS experience, including cloud architecture, security, and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of large, complex technical initiatives from start to finish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing secure, reliable, maintainable systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication, sound technical judgment, and a collaborative approach to solving difficult problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a U.S. person (U.S. citizen or lawful permanent resident) residing in the U.S.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS GovCloud, FedRAMP, regulated environments, or compliance-driven software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating with AI providers for SaaS applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extra Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a full-time, permanent position with competitive compensation, stock options, health benefits and a 401K match. The role can be worked remotely from anywhere in the United States.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Note&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Frequently cited statistics show that people who identify with historically marginalized groups are likely to apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. We encourage you to help us break that statistic and apply even if you don’t meet every single qualification—your potential is what matters most to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoLab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoLab, we help mechanical engineering teams bring life-changing products to market years sooner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build AI for engineers designing cars, medical devices, and jet engines. Products this complex aren&#39;t sketched and sent to production. Teams spend months on iterations, reviews, and tests, predicting how every part performs before anything is built. CoLab is where those reviews happen, and we capture the rationale behind every change. Other tools show what changed between versions. Only CoLab knows why. That&#39;s how our AI helps manufacturers like Bobcat, Triumph Motorcycles, and GE Appliances make better decisions, eliminate rework cycles, and get to market faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proudly based in St. John’s, Newfoundland, CoLab started with one customer in 2018. Since then we’ve raised a&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/ai-is-changing-engineering-colab-just-raised-72m-to-lead-the-transformation&quot;&gt; $72M Series C&lt;/a&gt;, been named the 57th fastest growing company in North America by Deloitte (&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/colab-ranked-number-57-fastest-growing-company-in-north-america-on-the-2025-deloitte-technology-fast-500&quot;&gt;Fast 500™&lt;/a&gt;), signed multi-year&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-bombardier-signs-contract-colab-ai-software/&quot;&gt; AI partnerships with companies like Bombardier&lt;/a&gt;, and grown to a team of 250+.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Software Forward Deployed Engineer to embed within our strategic customers and deliver on high-impact, technically complex customer projects. This includes scoping, building, and deploying complex integrations, product features and AI product features that connect customer systems to CoLab, accelerate adoption and increase customer return on investment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own delivery of key customer initiatives, working closely with our customer success, product, design and engineering teams, as well as leadership team stakeholders to remove blockers and deliver results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unlike a traditional software development role, FDEs must manage significant ambiguity, external team dynamics, and timeline pressure. If you like working directly with customers and shipping code to solve real, complex user problems with a high level agency and autonomy, then you will thrive in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery of strategic customer projects, from technical discovery through to production deployment and success measures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deploy complex system integrations, backend services, and data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with enterprise systems, including data lakes, identity management and access controls solutions, and Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) and Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up CoLab integrations and organize incoming data to enable use in features like AutoReview and Operator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with customers to understand needs, propose solutions, and guide adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop targeted solutions that meet the specific Customer&#39;s requirements whilst ensuring solutions are designed and developed with our broader customer base in mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring your extensive knowledge of our Customer&#39;s requirements back to the development team for learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Ideal Candidate&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re based in the United States and are comfortable working on site with our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve delivered complex technical solutions for projects where requirements were not clearly defined&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write clean, production-grade code in a variety of languages and consider yourself language agnostic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable working in unfamiliar environments - both technically and organizationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked with enterprise systems (e.g., data lakes, IdP, PLM, ERP, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can break down ambiguity, sequence work, and adjust scope without losing momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re confident leading deeply technical conversations with customer engineering or IT teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about delivering outcomes, not just writing code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a “go figure it out” mindset and can roll with the punches when things shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work embedding within customer environments as part of enterprise SaaS deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or integrating AI-powered features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with manufacturing or engineering data, processes, or systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with API-first products or developer platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Extra Details&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a full-time, permanent position with a competitive compensation package that includes, base salary and stock options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Includes extended health benefits, unlimited vacation, and 401k matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role can be be worked remotely from anywhere in the United States but regular travel is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizenship is required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
