&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at Lyft, data is at the core of every decision we make. It powers our business — helping us create great transportation experiences for our customers and providing insights into the effectiveness of our product launches and features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Data Engineer on Lyft’s Marketplace – Decision Apps team, you will own and evolve the data pipelines that power our top-line financial, pricing, and driver-related metrics. You will collaborate with Analytics, Data Science, and Engineering partners to design data models and architectures — proposing innovative ideas, evaluating multiple approaches, and implementing solutions grounded in fundamental engineering principles and rigorous data analysis. Your work will provide seamless access to the insights that drive Lyft’s success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of core data pipelines, ensuring resilience, optimal performance, timely delivery, data quality, and seamless onboarding of new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evolve data models and schemas to meet business and engineering requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain systems to monitor and enhance data quality and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop tools that support self-service management of data pipelines (ETL) and perform SQL tuning to optimize data processing performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the Data Engineering team’s technical roadmap, ensuring alignment with team and stakeholder goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, well-tested, and maintainable code, prioritizing scalability and cost efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct code reviews to uphold code quality standards and facilitate knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call rotations to maintain high availability and reliability of workflows and data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal and external partners to remove blockers, provide support, and achieve results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in data engineering as a hands-on Individual Contributor delivering features end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders (analytics, science, product, and engineering) to align data solutions with business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in data validation, analysis, and visualization for clear insight presentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in designing complex data models and resilient data pipelines, with solid understanding of analytical data modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in advanced SQL, capable of understanding intricate business logic and implementing custom solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong algorithmic foundation and hands-on coding skills in Python, Java, or similar languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of MPP systems and hands-on experience with ETL in Spark or similar technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data system design principles for data-intensive applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with workflow management tools (e.g., Airflow, Flyte, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional and stable working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The latest technology and equipment you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Potential to work remotely, including out of country (dependent on work authorizations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 calendar days for vacation and up to 5 paid sick days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is fully remote in Ukraine, however, employees are required to live and work in Ukraine in order to be qualified for this position.&lt;/strong&gt; #Remote&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Travel team helps people who travel for work choose Lyft, and grows business travel as a line of business, one of Lyft’s growth priorities. Our customers include individual riders and the companies that offer Lyft as an employee benefit, so the work spans consumer and B2B products. Since launching Lyft Business Rewards in 2025, we’ve seen strong traction with business travelers. Next, we want to make Lyft the most rewarding and reliable way to travel for work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team includes back-end, web, iOS, and Android engineers and works closely with product management, design, and data science. Our work touches the core rider experience, so we partner closely with many teams across Lyft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you’ll lead the team and its roadmap. You’ll own planning and delivery with your PM partner, guide technical direction through design reviews, and coach engineers. We’re looking for an engineering manager with a solid software background and experience leading engineers, who has shipped consumer or B2B2C products alongside product, design, and data partners. You can build trust with a team quickly, set a clear rhythm for planning and communication, and grow engineers into future tech leads.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive team execution by resolving blockers, mediating decision-making, and navigating ambiguity to keep the team moving with clarity and momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain operational excellence by implementing and upholding best practices for observability, reliability, and on-call processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams — Product, Marketing, Science, and Analytics — to define the team&#39;s strategic direction and roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure technical excellence through architecture reviews, proactive tech debt management, and hands-on engineering guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain team health by creating and refining team processes, fostering a supportive and inclusive culture, and managing resourcing needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop team member careers by matching them with the right opportunities, setting clear expectations, and delivering timely and actionable feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships across engineering teams to share learnings, align on standards, and identify collaboration opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business goals into clear engineering plans, helping the team understand the &quot;why&quot; behind their work and stay motivated by impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and address underperformance early, while consistently recognizing individual strengths and contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to hiring by partnering with recruiting, conducting interviews, and helping define and uphold the team&#39;s engineering bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. or M.S. in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of software development experience, with enough technical depth to engage credibly in architecture and design discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years of people management experience, with a demonstrated ability to grow engineers and build cohesive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering projects end-to-end in a fast-paced environment, balancing speed with quality and sustainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills — comfortable working alongside Product, Design, Science, and Analytics to align on priorities and drive shared outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in ambiguity, decompose complex problems, and bring structure and clarity to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a diverse set of engineering roles — backend, web, mobile, and/or data — is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a growth-focused team or org (incentives, messaging, ads) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to represent the team clearly to senior stakeholders and advocate effectively for resourcing and prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please submit your resume in English.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft’s engineering team is growing rapidly, and we are looking for engineering managers to help us scale. Our engineers are smart, flexible, and love solving difficult challenges.&amp;nbsp; Our engineers are smart, flexible, and love solving difficult challenges. They look to their managers for organizational transparency, career development, mentorship, and honest feedback. They move fast and ship code to production continuously, relying on their leadership to increase productivity by removing obstacles and keeping processes lean. Our engineering managers are people with diverse technical backgrounds and interests. As managers it is our job to remain curious and continuously deliver impact by driving our team’s technical direction and vision. We build teams that are inclusive, helpful, and have a strong sense of ownership for the things they build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft’s Infrastructure teams are responsible for building the foundational systems that engineers rely on in order to build stable, scalable, and efficient services. We build scalable infrastructure that helps software developers move fast, while still providing them with the flexibility they need to innovate within their teams. We are looking for experienced leaders to guide these teams as they create an exceptional development experience for all of Lyft. These are high leverage roles, as your work will have a multiplicative effect across Engineering, and contribute directly to Lyft’s overall stability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Engineering Manager for the Developer Environments team, you will lead a talented group of engineers responsible for building and maintaining critical infrastructure that enhances developer productivity and system reliability. The team builds and supports the environments where developers work and test as well as simulation systems and tools. Some of these systems are critical to the SDLC of engineers at Lyft, others ensure Lyft’s production services can handle the load of customer demand during peak events like New Years Eve, while optimizing for efficiency throughout the remainder of the year. You will play a key role in shaping the team’s vision, supporting their growth, and delivering impactful solutions for engineers throughout the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read more about some of the projects this team has worked on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://eng.lyft.com/scaling-productivity-on-microservices-at-lyft-part-3-extending-our-envoy-mesh-with-staging-fdaafafca82f&quot;&gt;Extending our Envoy mesh with staging overrides&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://eng.lyft.com/scaling-productivity-on-microservices-at-lyft-part-4-gating-deploys-with-automated-acceptance-4417e0ebc274&quot;&gt;Gating Deploys with Automated Acceptance Tests&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://eng.lyft.com/simulatedrides-how-lyft-uses-load-testing-to-ensure-reliable-service-during-peak-events-644dcb654454&quot;&gt;How Lyft uses load testing to ensure reliable service during peak events&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Infrastructure Engineering teams responsible for maintaining and improving our infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance feature development speed and reliability with service-level objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and guide the professional and technical development of your team members. Help develop their careers, and assign them to projects tailored to their skill levels, personalities, work styles, and professional goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build teams that are collaborative, inclusive, and respectful of each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide continuous feedback, support individuals on improving or optimizing their performance, and recognize the strengths and contributions of your team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create plans for prioritizing technical and resourcing challenges in your organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a balance between building sustainable, high-impact projects and shipping things quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instill a spirit of continuous improvement in the team’s code, architecture, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Lyft recruiting team to hire high potential candidates from diverse backgrounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with your engineers and stakeholders to maintain a prioritized backlog and create short term and long term goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your team’s deliverables and ensure we continue to ship scalable, highly-available products that delight our passengers and drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experience:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience as an Engineering Manager. Previous experience managing Infrastructure teams a bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a technical background and are able to contribute to planning and design discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proficient in one or more high-level programming language, such as Python, Go, Rust, or Javascript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on teams responsible for maintaining and operating production software and infrastructure at a large-scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are steadfastly focused on your customers, whether they are drivers, passengers, or other Lyft employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team of engineers and supporting them through career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built teams and products that scale with a company’s evolving needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working in a collaborative environment, and you’re committed to driving projects to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built teams that are motivated and value a strong sense of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting teams through planning, prioritization, and execution of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
